#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch15-evaluation-and-benchmarks.md:49
#: c5b347bb339e41be884f99fe9879563e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For the code-layer retrieval system (Chapter 12), the useful metrics are the"
" standard IR ones against a held-out test set of question/citation pairs: "
"nDCG@10, recall@10, MRR. For the prose-layer retrieval, these metrics apply "
"with a caveat: the ground truth is harder to label (a single question often "
"has multiple correct pages), and partial credit matters more. Both surfaces "
"benefit from the end-to-end answer-faithfulness metrics in RAGAS "
"{cite}`es2024ragas` and similar frameworks."
msgstr ""
"对代码层检索系统（第 12 章）而言，有用的指标就是那些标准的 IR 指标：在一份留出的 `(问题, 引用)` 对测试集上跑 "
"nDCG@10、recall@10、MRR。对文稿层检索，这些指标同样适用，但有一个注脚：ground truth "
"更难标注（同一个问题常常对应多个正确页面），并且“部分得分”更重要。两类面板都能从 RAGAS {cite}`es2024ragas` "
"及其同类框架里的“端到端 answer-faithfulness”指标中获益。"

